<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Kharistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">737</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-conquest-of-transoxiana">Muslim conquest of Transoxiana</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Kharistan was fought in December 737 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guzgan">Guzgan</a>, in present-day northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>. The Umayyad governor of Khurasan, Asad ibn Abdallah al-Qasri, surprised the Turgesh <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suluk">Suluk</a> and his allies as they raided south of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Oxus</a> and defeated them. The loss destroyed Suluk's prestige, he was murdered by a rival soon after, and the Turgesh fell into civil war, ending their threat to Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-kharistan.jpg" alt="Battle of Kharistan" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cplakidas · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Transoxiana_8th_century.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
